{"type":"message_start","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Machine\n- Apple M5 Max, 18 of 18 logical cores allocated\n- ceiling dram_bandwidth: 365 Gbyte/s\n- ceiling flops_dp: 643 GFLOP/s\n- ceiling flops_sp: 1.26 TFLOP/s\n\n## Diagnostic for `axpy` (line level)\n- share of the sampled time: 100%\n- no roofline placement: no flops_dp raw counter in this Run\n\n## Hot inner loop (static analysis of the instruction stream, insensitive to cache reuse)\n- 12 instructions per iteration, 16 FLOPs\n- vectorized: 100% of the FP instructions, 128-bit\n- 128 bytes loaded, 64 stored per iteration; 0 gathers\n\n## Samples by source line\n- line 5: 100%\n\n## Source (`triad-mid.c`, lines 2-8)\n```\n#include <stdlib.h>\n__attribute__((noinline)) void axpy(double a, const double *x, double *y, int n)\n{\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) y[i] = a * x[i] + y[i];\n}\nint main(void)\n{\n```\n\nExplain this behavior and suggest optimizations."}],"timestamp":1787502358444}}
